It looks entirely deliberate to me that 0 is a valid level for a
monster to be drained to. From the leveldraining code in
artifact_hit():

              if (mdef->m_lev == 0) {
                  *dmgptr = 2 * mdef->mhp + FATAL_DAMAGE_MODIFIER;
              } else {
                  int drain = rnd(8);
                  *dmgptr += drain;
                  mdef->mhpmax -= drain;
                  mdef->m_lev--;
                  drain /= 2;
                  if (drain) healup(drain, 0, FALSE, FALSE);
              }

And from the code for the spell of drain life in bhitm():

        if (mtmp->mhp <= 0 || mtmp->mhpmax <= 0 || mtmp->m_lev < 1)
            xkilled(mtmp, 1);
        else {
            mtmp->m_lev--;
            if (canseemon(mtmp))
                pline("%s suddenly seems weaker!", Monnam(mtmp));
        }

Once might be a bug; twice is intention.

